    ],
    "summary": "Timing favored Den of Thieves, who bought a higher‑valued WR23 while the market was still pricing McConkey above McLaurin. Avalanche sold the premium McConkey at a premium and bought two lower‑valued pieces, effectively cashing in. The deal makes sense because Avalanche needed a healthy starter now, and Den of Thieves can absorb McConkey’s foot issue with depth at WR. Den of Thieves wins this trade, though he assumes the risk of McConkey’s lingering questionability.",
    "headline": "Devin and Adam"
