     }
    ],
    "summary": "By swapping a veteran WR for a veteran RB, each manager signals a shift in positional focus for the season. Eastside Express is saying he values a more reliable WR slot, while Crosstown Comets is indicating a need to bolster his backfield depth. Eastside Express wins this trade, acquiring the higher‑valued Mike Evans, and Crosstown Comets takes on the lower‑valued Aaron Jones. The move leaves Crosstown Comets with a modest downgrade in overall package value, while Eastside Express gains a clear upgrade in weekly upside.",
    "headline": "Ethan and Tyler"
